DB Browser's SqliteTableModel loads rows via a RowLoader that inherits
QThread and uses std::async, std::mutex and std::condition_variable to
run row fetches on a worker thread. Qt-wasm doesn't ship pthreads, so
QThread::run() never fires and std::async's async policy is a no-op:
opening a table just shows nothing because rows are queued to a worker
that never runs.

On wasm, run everything synchronously on the calling thread. Signals
still fire through Qt::QueuedConnection so UI updates happen on the
next event-loop tick.

